{
    "$comment": [
        "Register of every artefact in the docs site that is GENERATED rather than written.",
        "",
        "A generated artefact is committed to the repository and refreshed on demand, so the",
        "docs build stays a plain Docusaurus build with no monorepo dependency, and a stale",
        "diagram shows up as a diff in review instead of drifting silently.",
        "",
        "Read and checked by `blong-dev docs` (tools/blong-dev/src/commands/docs.ts):",
        "  blong-dev docs list                 the register, with each destination present or missing",
        "  blong-dev docs generate [--only id] run the generators and write the artefacts",
        "  blong-dev docs check                regenerate, compare, restore; non-zero when stale",
        "",
        "Fields:",
        "  id          stable identifier, also used by --only and by the generic GENERATED marker",
        "  kind        'file'          the generator owns the whole destination file",
        "              'mermaid-inline' the generator rewrites only the region between a marker pair",
        "              'png'           a screenshot: `check` only verifies it exists and is non-empty",
        "                              (PNG bytes depend on font rendering, so it is not compared,",
        "                              and its generator is not run \u2014 content is reviewed instead)",
        "  destination repository-relative path of the file the artefact lives in",
        "  marker      for 'mermaid-inline' only: the text between BEGIN and END, i.e. the value of",
        "              `<id>` in `<!-- BEGIN <marker> -->` ... `<!-- END <marker> -->`",
        "  package     repository-relative package the generator runs in (its working directory)",
        "  command     shell command that regenerates the artefact, run in `package`; a command",
        "              that runs tap directly must pass `--allow-incomplete-coverage` (and usually",
        "              `--coverage-report=none`), because the repository gates suites at 100%",
        "              coverage and a single file run on its own can never reach it \u2014 without the",
        "              flag the generator exits 1 on a suite that passed. `blong-dev test` passes",
        "              the same flags for the same reason.",
        "  doc         for 'mermaid-inline' only: the documentation page that embeds it",
        "",
        "The generators are deterministic by design: a call is placed by the counter path its",
        "caller assigned and no count comes from the clock, so regenerating an up-to-date artefact",
        "is a no-op and `check` can compare rather than guess. Do not hand-edit a registered",
        "destination \u2014 the next `generate` overwrites it, and `check` fails until it does."
    ],
    "version": 1,
    "artifacts": [
        {
            "id": "flows.artifact",
            "kind": "file",
            "destination": "core/semantic-log/docs/observed-flows.md",
            "package": "core/semantic-log",
            "command": "SEMANTIC_LOG_UPDATE_DIAGRAMS=1 ./node_modules/.bin/tap --allow-incomplete-coverage --coverage-report=none test/flow/observedFlows.test.ts"
        },
        {
            "id": "flows.transfer-single",
            "kind": "mermaid-inline",
            "destination": "docs/blong/docs/patterns/semantic-log-flows.md",
            "marker": "OBSERVED FLOWS: transfer.single",
            "package": "core/semantic-log",
            "command": "SEMANTIC_LOG_UPDATE_DIAGRAMS=1 ./node_modules/.bin/tap --allow-incomplete-coverage --coverage-report=none test/flow/observedFlows.test.ts",
            "doc": "patterns/semantic-log-flows.md"
        },
        {
            "id": "flows.transfer-inter",
            "kind": "mermaid-inline",
            "destination": "docs/blong/docs/patterns/semantic-log-flows.md",
            "marker": "OBSERVED FLOWS: transfer.inter",
            "package": "core/semantic-log",
            "command": "SEMANTIC_LOG_UPDATE_DIAGRAMS=1 ./node_modules/.bin/tap --allow-incomplete-coverage --coverage-report=none test/flow/observedFlows.test.ts",
            "doc": "patterns/semantic-log-flows.md"
        },
        {
            "id": "layers.activation",
            "kind": "mermaid-inline",
            "destination": "docs/blong/docs/concepts/layer.md",
            "marker": "LAYER ACTIVATION",
            "package": "core/blong-lib",
            "command": "BLONG_UPDATE_DOCS=1 ./node_modules/.bin/tap --allow-incomplete-coverage --coverage-report=none layersActivation.test.ts",
            "doc": "concepts/layer.md"
        },
        {
            "id": "realm.observed-flows",
            "kind": "file",
            "destination": "core/blong-realm/docs/observedFlows.md",
            "package": "core/blong-realm",
            "command": "BLONG_REGENERATE_DIAGRAMS=1 node --run playwright -- test/blong.play.ts --update-snapshots"
        },
        {
            "id": "realm.observed-kind-union",
            "kind": "file",
            "destination": "core/blong-realm/docs/observedKindUnion.md",
            "package": "core/blong-realm",
            "command": "BLONG_REGENERATE_DIAGRAMS=1 node --run playwright -- test/blong.play.ts --update-snapshots"
        },
        {
            "id": "gateway.observed-flows",
            "kind": "file",
            "destination": "realm/blong-gateway/docs/observedFlows.md",
            "package": "realm/blong-gateway",
            "command": "BLONG_REGENERATE_DIAGRAMS=1 node --run playwright -- test/observedFlow.play.ts --update-snapshots"
        },
        {
            "id": "gateway.observed-merge-flow",
